cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use do-math, please cite it using the metadata in this file. To cite the published knowledge base of the first run, cite the Zenodo record listed under references."
type: software
title: "do-math"
abstract: "do-math runs research on one mathematical proposition through many fresh AI sessions that share no conversation. Each piece of work is produced by one session, developed into a record by a second session, and assessed by a third; published records are immutable and carry their assessments. A root proposition counts as settled only when an independently recompiled Lean proof has been checked against the exact statement."
authors:
